=== ISSUE ===
Title: create_arena and decline_challenge send JSON; the spec wants a form, and arena conditions use the wrong field names

The Lichess API spec (https://github.com/lichess-org/api/blob/906d1a6e93ca1ba4b65c9decb3077f2431c6d55a/doc/specs/lichess-api.yaml) defines `POST /api/tournament` and `POST /api/challenge/{challengeId}/decline` as `application/x-www-form-urlencoded`. Both tools send JSON.

`create_arena` also sends entry conditions as `{ conditions: { minRating, maxRating, nbRatedGame, teamMember } }`. The spec's fields are `conditions.minRating.rating`, `conditions.maxRating.rating`, `conditions.nbRatedGame.nb` and `conditions.teamMember.teamId`, so rating, games and team restrictions can't be applied as sent.

=== PR ===
Title: fix: send create_arena and decline_challenge as form bodies
Body:
Closes #<issue>

- `create_arena` posts a form and maps `conditions` to the spec's dotted fields; unset conditions are omitted.
- `decline_challenge` posts `reason` as a form field.

